    feat: add worktree-reap-data-loss + fast-forward-push-reject classes; widen docs-count-drift; sync doc counts. Addresses LORE-034, LORE-035, LORE-033.
    
    Two new curated classes in the closed SEED_CLASSES registry so the
    2026-09-26 discovery stress test phrasings classify instead of falling
    back to unclassified (LORE-017/LORE-032 closed-registry precedent):
    
    - lore/classes.py: worktree-reap-data-loss seed (reap/classified-merged
      phrasings anchored on an un-committed-work marker: zero-commit, no
      commits, never committed — a healthy post-merge reap never fires it) and
      fast-forward-push-reject seed (every pattern requires a divergence
      marker: non-fast-forward / diverged / advanced — an auth-shaped
      "permission denied" refusal never fires it). LORE-035 rides here:
      docs-count-drift gains three signature patterns covering the
      "docs say N tests, actual count on <ref> is M" shape and the
      "documentation lists N but the real count is M" close variant; keywords
      and description untouched.
    - lore/classes.py (shared-checkout-collision): narrowed the broad
      "worktree deleted" alternative to require sibling/collision context so
      it cannot swallow the reap-data-loss phrasings in registry order (first
      class wins); "worktree reap" and "collision" alternatives keep the
      existing fixtures green.
    - lore/compiler.py: checks / recovery ladders / guardrails / evidence
      trails for both new classes, following the LORE-017 per-class shape.
      All seeded checks are read_only=True and gate-approved.
    - lore/validate.py: `git fetch` added to the read-only git verbs — it is
      network read-only on the REMOTE (updates remote-tracking refs only,
      never local branches/index/tree); the fast-forward-push-reject runbook
      needs it to read the true origin divergence. pull/push/reset/checkout
      stay refused (test_unmarked_write_shaped_command_still_refuses pins it).
    - tests/test_lore034_reap_and_push_classes.py: canonical inputs 1/2/3,
      shape variants for each, near-miss guards ("worktree merged and removed
      after merge confirmation" stays off the reap class; "push rejected:
      permission denied (publickey)" stays off the push-reject class;
      "README claims 148 tests but the suite shows 297" regression pin for
      the widened docs seed), out-of-vocabulary unclassified pin, and
      registry-count assertions DERIVED from SEED_CLASSES (base + 2, registry
      = seeds + 1) per the LORE-017 derived-count precedent.
    - tests/test_classes.py: SEED_CLASS_IDS gains the two new ids so the
      derived registry pin stays exact.
    - README.md / docs/INSTALL.md / skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md /
      scripts/test-count.txt (LORE-033 count sync): "10 failure classes" ->
      13 (the LORE-032 wave had already left line 142 one behind), class-id
      list carries all 13, "11 curated classes" -> 13, test-count literals
      297 -> 309 (18 test files), canonical count file 297 -> 309.
    
    Verified: uv run pytest -q (309 passed), ruff check + format --check
    clean, sh scripts/check-test-count.sh PASS (canonical=309 matches
    live=309), classify() on all three stress inputs lands the right class at
    confidence 0.90, both near-miss inputs stay off their neighboring classes.
